  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Find the shortest distance between the point $(4,-1)$ and the line $x=-2.$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's sketch the given situation.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14224553/assets/ae9c7b44a3e246fb6e0e9f90c1288ef42814c22d705c944e46fe0eb890a5a998.png)\n\nSince the line $x=-2$ is a vertical line, the shortest distance between this line and the point $(4,-1)$ is given by the absolute value of the difference between the $x$-coordinate of the point and $-2.$ \n\nSo, the shortest distance is\n\n$$\nd=|4-(-2)|=6.\n$$",
